Id: path007
Severity: FAIL, WARN, INFO
Category: accounts
Check: check_path

A directory on a user's PATH can be written by its group or by any
user. Whoever can write the directory can drop in a Trojan horse under
the name of a command the user runs. Remove the write permission, or
take the directory out of the PATH. As with path006, the old suffixed
entries are kept for old reports.
